Laurence Gordon writes:
>  What's the best thing to polymorph into?
 
This is real situation dependent and depends on what your problems
are.  But if you're wandering around with no particular problems,
wearing a ring of polymorph control, and you stumble into a polymorph
trap--
  Vampire Lord and Master Lich are pretty good.  They have good stats,
they can carry a pretty good pack, they have some pretty good
intrinsics, and (importantly) they can wear the same armor as a human.

  If you have a chance to disrobe beforehand (or you have spare armor
and cloaks) then a Xorn is a very powerful creature and has this
amazing ability to walk thru walls.  This can be particularly nice in
the castle level if you don't have any way of levitating over the
trapdoors.  One major warning -- don't get trapped in the dirt without
a pickaxe or a means of teleporting out.  

  When polypiling, one way to get a mess of spellbooks is to turn into
a stone giant, pick up all the boulders on the level and put them in
the pile, polymorph them into statues and hit the pile with a wand of
striking.

  If you're a nymph you can remove a ball and chain.  Many other
monsters have nifty intrinsics; get into exploration mode, wish for a
ring of polymorph and a ring of polymorph control, and play around
with it.  I mean, being a fire elemental isn't that useful, but it's
kind of fun.  Werecreatures can summon help, but you may find that
having a half dozen tame wargs is more of a hassle than it's worth.

